  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In general from left to right in a period, ionisation enthalpy increases due to effective nuclear charge increases. but due to extra stability of half filled and full filled electronic configuration, required ionisation enthalpy is more from neighbouring elements.<br />i.e. first ionisation enthalpy order is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Si</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math></p>",
